    <item>
      <title>Hey, Listen! Navi in BotW (WiiU)</title>
      <author>zapiltar</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/742763</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/742763#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">f2f582f4a8f4ac701964b88722ba00ea74e3be4e</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:00:14 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6afeec4094f70.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6afeec40a6efc.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6afeec40d288b.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; TotK Edition Parity&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Feature/behavior parity with the 1.0 TotK version.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Hey, Listen!&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;br&gt;This mod brings Navi, the Hero of Time's trusty companion to Breath of the Wild!&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Navi takes over the game's ZL targeting, both the soft lock white arrow, and the hard lock orange arrow. When you target a hostile npc she glows orange, targeting a friendly npc she glows green.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When you aren't in combat or chatting with people, she floats over Link's left shoulder occasionally chattering. If Link stands around long enough Navi will get bored and start flying around in the vicinity.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;During cutscenes or dialog, Navi hides in Link's hat/hair until the player regains control of Link; this is to avoid any odd behavior and maintain some continuity with her missing in prerendered cutscenes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;She will also hide when Link freefalls, rides a horse, and during fast travel.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;u&gt;Installation Guide&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Cemu Standalone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Copy the &lt;i&gt;Navi &lt;/i&gt;folder from the zip into Cemu's &lt;i&gt;graphicPacks &lt;/i&gt;folder&lt;br&gt;- In the Graphic Packs menu, check Navi; you can change the mod's settings here too&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Cemu UKMM&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Unzip the _ModManager.zip&lt;br&gt;- In UKMM, select &lt;i&gt;Navi (UKMM).zip&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;and install&lt;br&gt;- Hit deploy after applying your other mods, and move the UKMM Graphic Pack to the &lt;i&gt;graphicPacks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;folder&lt;br&gt;- In the Graphic Packs menu, check UKMM and Navi (Code); you can&lt;br&gt;change the mod's settings in Navi (Code)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Settings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The settings can be changed during gameplay with no restart required through the graphics pack menu.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Tested&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;This mod was made and tested on BotW 1.5.0 on the Cemu emulator version 2.6&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;AI Contributions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;Claude Code was used for the reverse engineering and as a programming assistant to understand the game memory and code addresses that are used to hook Navi to each of Link's and the game states, trigger sounds, and change npc states.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Planned Features&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Known Issues&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;Other Releases&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/743088"&gt;Switch 1.6.0/1.9.0 Version&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/744196"&gt;TotK 1.2.1/1.4.3 Version&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/navi_botw_wiiu_v21.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/navi_botw_wiiu_v21_modmanager.zip" type="application/zip"/>
