    <item>
      <title>Hyrule Stash</title>
      <author>Faen90</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/740413</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/740413#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">19598c1e72f55a59f29082b6e50d48df14e1f174</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:52:25 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6afa4505d1f54.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6afa43dd83b30.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6afa43da5ede1.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6afa43da7caa5.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6afa43dbe0f7f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; Stash 1.1.0 – A Proper Treasure Trunk&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Stash gets a whole new look. It’s now a hand-painted traveller’s trunk built to sit naturally in Hyrule: oak boards, leather straps with brass buckles, brass corners and iron handles. Walk up and activate it and the lid swings open with the game’s own chest sound, showing a hero’s hoard inside: the Hylian Shield, Guardian and Royal swords, gems, apples and rupees. When you’re done, it shuts again. The compendium picture and key item icon show the new trunk too. Reinstall the mod part to update; the graphic pack hasn’t changed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Change&lt;/em&gt;: [Feature] The stash is a new traveller’s trunk, painted to match the game’s own props: oak boards, leather straps with brass buckles and tips, brass corners and hasp, and iron handles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Change&lt;/em&gt;: [Feature] The lid opens when you use the stash and shuts when you’re done, with the game’s chest sounds. This works for placed stashes and the one summoned with the key item.&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Change&lt;/em&gt;: [Feature] Inside lies a hero’s hoard: the Hylian Shield, Guardian and Royal swords, arrows, gems, apples and rupees, all the game’s own models.&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Change&lt;/em&gt;: [Improvement] Much sharper textures, and colours that suit the game’s lighting.&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Change&lt;/em&gt;: [Improvement] New Hyrule Compendium picture and key item icon showing the new trunk.&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Change&lt;/em&gt;: [Other] Reinstall the mod part for this; the graphic pack is unchanged. In UKMM, close and reopen UKMM before reinstalling.&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Stash: item storage for Hyrule&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
Never drop a good weapon again. The &lt;b&gt;Stash&lt;/b&gt; keeps whatever you put in it: weapons, bows, shields, armor, food and materials. Take them out again whenever you like, exactly as they went in. Everything happens inside the game, through its own screens.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Features&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;26 stashes around Hyrule&lt;/b&gt;, beside the stables and in the settlements. Walk up to one and &lt;i&gt;Access Stash&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;One stash, reached from anywhere.&lt;/b&gt; Every stash opens the same hold, so put things in at Kakariko and take them out at Rito Village.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;The Stash key item.&lt;/b&gt; Use the stash at 5 different stables to earn it, then open it from your key items and a stash appears in front of Link. (Or have it from the start: see &lt;i&gt;Settings&lt;/i&gt;.)&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stash Items&lt;/b&gt; uses the game's own inventory screen, with all its tabs. For a stack, choose how many or &lt;i&gt;All of them&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Take out&lt;/b&gt; by kind: Weapons, Bows &amp; Arrows, Shields, Armor, Food or Materials. The list shows each item's icon, its stats (attack, guard, defense, hearts) and how many are stashed. Press &lt;b&gt;Y&lt;/b&gt; to sort it by type, stats or quantity.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Everything comes back exactly as it went in:&lt;/b&gt; a weapon's durability and bonus, a dish's effect, hearts and ingredients. For a dish, the panel shows what it was made with.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Holds a lot:&lt;/b&gt; 999 kinds of stackable items, up to 99,999 each, plus 999 weapons, bows, shields, armor pieces, dishes and elixirs. Modded items work too.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;In the Hyrule Compendium.&lt;/b&gt; Photograph a stash with the Camera rune to add it under &lt;i&gt;Treasure&lt;/i&gt;, as the last entry, so no other entry's number changes.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Each save slot has its own stash&lt;/b&gt;, kept in a file of its own beside the save. Loading an older save brings back that save's stash.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Breath of the Wild for &lt;b&gt;Wii U, updated to 1.5.0 (v208)&lt;/b&gt;, on &lt;b&gt;Cemu&lt;/b&gt; (tested with Cemu 2.6 on the EU release).&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;BCML&lt;/b&gt; or &lt;b&gt;UKMM&lt;/b&gt;, to install the mod and merge it with your other mods.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;The DLC&lt;/b&gt; for the stashes placed in the world (the key item works without it).&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Installing&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&lt;ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;In &lt;b&gt;BCML&lt;/b&gt; or &lt;b&gt;UKMM&lt;/b&gt;, install &lt;code&gt;BotW Storage Chest (install in BCML).zip&lt;/code&gt; and apply (remerge).&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Copy the &lt;code&gt;BotW Storage Chest&lt;/code&gt; graphics pack folder into Cemu's &lt;code&gt;graphicPacks&lt;/code&gt; folder and tick it in Cemu's graphic packs list.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Start the game. Both halves are needed: the mod adds the stash, its screens and texts; the graphics pack makes them work.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Updating&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
Install both halves of the new version, and replace the graphics pack folder.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;BCML&lt;/b&gt;: update the mod, or remove the old one and install the new one.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;UKMM&lt;/b&gt;: uninstall the old version first, then install the new one. UKMM's &lt;i&gt;Update&lt;/i&gt; keeps the old files.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Settings&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
In Cemu's graphic packs list, &lt;i&gt;Stash key item&lt;/i&gt;:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Earned&lt;/b&gt; (default): use the stash at 5 different stables, and the game hands you the key item.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;From the start&lt;/b&gt;: Link gets it straight away.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Compatibility&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;It only adds to the game, so BCML or UKMM merges it with your other mods.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Made to go with the &lt;b&gt;Crafting Project&lt;/b&gt;: the stashes stand beside its anvils. The Crafting Project isn't required.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;The stash itself adds nothing to your save file, so it won't push a save past the game's limit. The compendium entry adds 3 small flags, as every compendium entry has.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Removing the mod&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;Take everything out of the stash first.&lt;/b&gt; The stash files stay beside your saves and come back if you install the mod again.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Known limits&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Wii U v1.5.0 (v208) only; no Switch version.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Texts are in English in every language.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
